# Voice Transcription Plugin Guide

## Overview
This is a Tauri plugin that provides voice transcription and dictation capabilities using OpenAI's Whisper model. The plugin was extracted from the Juno Voice Controlled Computer Use Agent and is now a standalone, reusable component.

## Plugin Structure

### Rust Plugin
The core Rust implementation is in [tauri-plugin-voice-transcription/](mdc:tauri-plugin-voice-transcription):
- [src/lib.rs](mdc:tauri-plugin-voice-transcription/src/lib.rs) - Plugin initialization with Tauri 2.0 Builder pattern
- [src/controller.rs](mdc:tauri-plugin-voice-transcription/src/controller.rs) - Core VoiceController with audio recording/transcription logic
- [src/commands.rs](mdc:tauri-plugin-voice-transcription/src/commands.rs) - Tauri commands with proper generic bounds
- [src/error.rs](mdc:tauri-plugin-voice-transcription/src/error.rs) - Custom error types
- [src/config.rs](mdc:tauri-plugin-voice-transcription/src/config.rs) - Configuration struct

### TypeScript API
The TypeScript bindings are in [tauri-plugin-voice-transcription-api/](mdc:tauri-plugin-voice-transcription-api):
- [src/index.ts](mdc:tauri-plugin-voice-transcription-api/src/index.ts) - Main API exports
- [src/react.ts](mdc:tauri-plugin-voice-transcription-api/src/react.ts) - React hook for easy integration

## Key Technical Details

### Audio Processing
- Uses CPAL for cross-platform audio recording
- Automatically resamples audio to 16kHz (Whisper's requirement) using Rubato
- Supports both F32 and I16 sample formats
- Real-time partial transcription with 1.5s buffer chunks

### Thread Safety
- VoiceController is marked as `Send + Sync`
- All Tauri commands require `R: Runtime + Send + 'static` bounds
- Audio processing runs in a separate thread with channel communication

### Event System
Events use the `voice-transcription:` namespace:
- `voice-transcription:dictation-started`
- `voice-transcription:dictation-stopped`
- `voice-transcription:partial-result`
- `voice-transcription:final-result`

## Common Issues and Solutions

### Generic Type Bounds
If you see errors about `R cannot be sent between threads safely`, add `Send + 'static` bounds:
```rust
pub async fn command<R: tauri::Runtime + Send + 'static>(app: tauri::AppHandle<R>) -> Result<(), String>
```

### Plugin Setup
The setup closure in Tauri 2.0 takes two parameters:
```rust
.setup(move |app, _api| { /* ... */ })
```

### Missing State
Commands expect VoiceController to be managed. If not initialized, commands will fail. Always check initialization in `lib.rs`.

## Integration Example
See [examples/integration.md](mdc:tauri-plugin-voice-transcription/examples/integration.md) for migrating from internal implementation to the plugin.

## Dependencies
- whisper-rs 0.11.0 (Whisper model inference)
- cpal 0.15 (Audio recording)
- rubato 0.14.1 (Audio resampling)
- hound 3.5 (WAV file handling)
